Subject: [PATCH 1/1] N8 (Round-11): per-residue alternate-conformer selection
 policy
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds an opt-in per_residue altloc policy to the ingestion processor,
sharing one selector for both the PDB and mmCIF paths:

- per_atom (DEFAULT, unchanged): one conformer per atom, highest
  occupancy, ties keep first-in-file — the P0 item 6 invariant,
  byte-for-byte preserved (existing 3ERD assertions still pass).
- per_residue (new, opt-in via altloc_policy='per_residue'): choose ONE
  altloc ID per residue by TOTAL occupancy (first-seen ID on ties),
  keep blank-altloc shared atoms plus the chosen conformer's atoms.
  Prevents chimera residues that mix atom sets from different
  conformers when per-atom occupancies disagree.

Both policies guarantee exactly one atom per (chain, residue,
atom_name), so downstream consumers (LAW-130/155/200) are unaffected.
The engine DEFAULT stays per_atom: flipping it changes measurement
semantics and is owner-gated.

Tests: backend/tests/test_altloc_per_residue.py (12) + existing
test_altloc_selection.py (8) all pass. Full suite on this branch:
4 failed / 514 passed / 5 skipped — the 4 TestUsageWidget failures are
pre-existing at base ebc1fd79 in this environment (verified without
this patch) and unrelated to conformer selection.

Fresh implementation; the original N8 branch tip e9985c6 was lost with
the prior sandbox reset and is not restored or claimed here. Delivered
as a patch only (owner-gated merge); base
science/p0-correctness-2026-10-19 @ ebc1fd79.
